WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.276 --> 00:00:05.401
For most of us, January 
was a normal month at school.

00:00:05.401 --> 00:00:09.435
We learned together, we ate together, 
we played together.

00:00:09.435 --> 00:00:12.047
We hung out with each other every day.

00:00:12.047 --> 00:00:15.831
But as the coronavirus spread, 
our world was upended.

00:00:15.831 --> 00:00:20.281
In February, hundreds of millions of us
lost access to our schools.

00:00:20.281 --> 00:00:24.661
By the end of March, nearly every school
on Earth was closed.

00:00:24.661 --> 00:00:27.915
Closing schools 
creates distance between us.

00:00:27.915 --> 00:00:29.875
The distance slows the virus.

00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:32.075
It reduces hospital visits.

00:00:32.075 --> 00:00:34.163
It saves lives.

00:00:34.163 --> 00:00:36.483
We're proud to help flatten the curve,

00:00:36.483 --> 00:00:40.798
but now we need your help to keep 
the pandemic from flattening our spirits.

00:00:40.798 --> 00:00:42.530
Here's how you can help:

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:46.100
It's graduation season for millions 
of students throughout the world.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.130
We can't attend or support 
2020 graduations in person,

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.747
but that doesn't mean billions of us

00:00:52.747 --> 00:00:56.357
can't support the graduating 
classes of 2020 online.

00:00:56.357 --> 00:00:59.737
We need your help, graduates 
and supporters of graduates,

00:00:59.737 --> 00:01:04.301
to make this year a worldwide celebration 
of the hopes, the dreams,

00:01:04.301 --> 00:01:09.623
the ideas, and the futures of an entire 
generation of young people.

00:01:09.623 --> 00:01:13.973
With support from TED, we've outlined 
all the ways you can get involved

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.857
with this worldwide celebration here.

00:01:15.857 --> 00:01:20.548
We are the students whose lives 
have been impacted by COVID-19.

00:01:20.548 --> 00:01:24.585
Together, our ideas will define 
the world future.

00:01:24.585 --> 00:01:30.445
Visit TED.COM/GRADUATION to sign up 
and support our future today.

